        "id": 81798,
        "name": "pwatson1974",
        "username": "pwatson1974",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-14T21:53:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I tend to order the rpocess of damage as:</p><p>1) Select target</p><p>2) Determine damage type. Anything that modifes type is simltneous with everything else that does.</p><p>3) Determine immnity. If immune, stop.</p><p>4) Apply modifiers to the damage total. These are simltaneous, so can be applied in any order. I tend to break on initator and on target modifiers separtely and do the former first. If damage is 0, stop.</p><p>5) Redirect and return to step 1 if is a change of target. All redirections are simltaneous.</p><p>6) Apply any prevent damage features, or convert damage to healing.</p><p>7) Reduce targets hit points by damage total.</p><p>8) If target has hit points left, continue with any effect that applies after damage is dealt, such as the Chairman's retributive damage or Isothermic Transducer's second strike.</p><p>This is in no way backed up by the rules, just how I conceptualise the damage process.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
