        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-14T21:59:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"pwatson1974\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/48/1925_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> pwatson1974:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I tend to order the rpocess of damage as:1) Select target2) Determine damage type. Anything that modifes type is simltneous with everything else that does.3) Determine immnity. If immune, stop.4) Apply modifiers to the damage total. These are simltaneous, so can be applied in any order. I tend to break on initator and on target modifiers separtely and do the former first. If damage is 0, stop.5) Redirect and return to step 1 if is a change of target. All redirections are simltaneous.6) Apply any prevent damage features, or convert damage to healing.7) Reduce targets hit points by damage total.8) If target has hit points left, continue with any effect that applies after damage is dealt, such as the Chairman's retributive damage or Isothermic Transducer's second strike.</p>\n<p>This is in no way backed up by the rules, just how I conceptualise the damage process.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Theres the thing though, it actually&nbsp;<em>is</em> backed up by the rules, at least it is if I am seeing things right. That is not an incorrect way to resolve it.</p>",
