      {
        "id": 81800,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-14T22:07:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>I do not like the idea of implicit triggers, as Static effects seem officially to not have them (not expressly stated, but the static effects don't have timing definitely leads that way).</span></p><p>&nbsp;I have tried to reconcile the idea that Fortitude and SHD can be simultaneous effects, and Fortitude not have timing.</p><p>That is how I came to my current operating stance on timing static and triggered effects:</p><p>Static effects never have timing issues with other static effects, you don't need to time them or resolve them as such, you just need to do he math. &nbsp;This is largely because static effects do not oppose each other, a +1 and -1 don't fight to see who gets applied, they both apply for a change of 0. &nbsp;Conditional triggers like SHD and redirection triggered by amount of damage can conflict, and in those circumstances the application of a static effect and the triggering of a triggered effect can have simultaneous timing.</p><p>This is important because unlike conditional static eff<span>ects, conditional triggered effects do not recheck. &nbsp;Imbued Fire's bonus to fire damage and Micro Targetting Computer can apply their effects, then unaply them, no conditional trigger does that. &nbsp;If Super Human rechecked once it reduced damage it would just endlessly loop on damage of 5 or 6, constantly reducing then unreducing than reducing again.</span></p><p>An interesting test of conditional triggers, and the timing of different effects would be the following progression:</p><p>Fanatic has Divine Focus ans Sacrosanct Martyr in play, and the&nbsp;<span>twist the&nbsp;</span><span>ether on her, Baron Blade has elemental redistributor and a Mobile Defense Platform out.</span></p><p><span>1. &nbsp;Fanatic discards at the start of her turn to deal Baron Blade 2 radiant damage.</span></p><p><span>2. &nbsp;That damage is Fire and increased to 3 due to IF.</span></p><p><span>3. &nbsp;Because that damage is fire Baron Blade redirects it (to Fanatic for our purposes)</span></p><p><span>4. &nbsp;Visionary uses Twist the Ether to change the damage to Radiant, which reduces it to 2 (losing IF bonus), then increases it one to hit Fanatic for 3 radiant damage. &nbsp;Lets divine focus go away.</span></p><p><span>5. &nbsp;Fanatic sacrosanct Martyr's, dealing herself 5+1 radiant damage through TtE.</span></p><p><span>6. &nbsp;Fanatic deals the Mobile Defense Platform 10 damage, destroying it.</span></p><p>Is this a legal turn under the current rules?</p><p>Could Visionary wait till the damage is redirected to use Twist the Ether? (I don't see any reason she couldn't, since it is still Fanatic's damage)</p><p>If Visionary changed the damage would it then not be redirected by the Baron's Elemental redistributor and do nothing to the immune to damage Baron Blade. &nbsp;(this would only be the case if conditional triggered effects can recheck their requirements and untrigger, which I would say no to)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:04:21.387Z",
